1 REM FBCS PRT-0230
2 REM CLAIM A-11.4.4.1-02
3 REM TYPE INPUT
100 REM PROMPT AND ELAPSED IN INPUT #0, LINE INPUT #0, MAT INPUT #0 AND MAT LINE INPUT #0 WORK AS IN THE
102 REM STATEMENTS WITHOUT A CHANNEL (11.4.4.1 L.8110-8114, 11.4.4.6 L.8205-8209, 10.2.4.1 L.5154-5176):
104 REM THE PROMPT IS WRITTEN BEFORE THE REPLY IS READ, AND THE ELAPSED VARIABLE GETS A POSITIVE VALUE
106 REM (A CLOCK IS AVAILABLE). THE REPLIES ARE IN PRT-0230.IN; THE OUTPUT IS IN PRT-0230.OUT.
110 OPTION BASE 1
120 DIM V(2)
130 DECLARE STRING W$(2)
140 INPUT #0, PROMPT "N:", ELAPSED T1: N
150 PRINT N; SGN(T1)
160 LINE INPUT #0, PROMPT "L:", ELAPSED T2: A$
170 PRINT A$; SGN(T2)
180 MAT INPUT #0, PROMPT "M:", ELAPSED T3: V
190 PRINT V(1); V(2); SGN(T3)
200 MAT LINE INPUT #0, PROMPT "W:", ELAPSED T4: W$
210 PRINT W$(1); W$(2); SGN(T4)
220 END
